By the definition of auxiliary SNNs, we have three observations. First, $\|\mathbf{v}^\text{auxiliary}_d(t+dt)-\mathbf{v}^\text{ideal}(t)\|_2=\|\mathbf{v}^\text{super}(t+dt)-\mathbf{v}^\text{ideal}(t)\|_2=O(\tau\cdot n\cdot\lambda_{\max})$. Second, there exists $0\leq t'<t$ such that $\mathbf{v}^\text{auxiliary}_d(t)=\mathbf{v}^\text{super}(t')$ and $\Gamma(\mathbf{v}^\text{ideal}(t'))\neq\Gamma(\mathbf{v}^\text{ideal}(t))$. That is, we also have $\|\mathbf{v}^\text{auxiliary}_d(t)-\mathbf{v}^\text{ideal}(t')\|_2=\|\mathbf{v}^\text{super}(t')-\mathbf{v}^\text{ideal}(t)\|_2=O(\tau\cdot n\cdot\lambda_{\max})$. Finally, since $\Gamma(\mathbf{v}^\text{ideal}(t'))\neq\Gamma(\mathbf{v}^\text{ideal}(t))$, by Lemma~\ref{lem:ideal SNN dynamics}, we have $\mathbf{b}^\top\left(\mathbf{v}^\text{ideal}(t)-\mathbf{v}^\text{ideal}(t')\right)=\Omega(\|\mathbf{b}\|_2\cdot\frac{\gamma(A)}{n\cdot\lambda_{\max}})$. Combine the three we have 
